Hi,

I have just created updated installation images for Debian Ports.

With these images, the issue with the console not working on powerpc
and ppc64 has finally been fixed such that an installation should work
normally. At least a very quick test on QEMU with an emulated PowerMac G5
worked fine.

FWIW, on alpha, installation should fail due to the vim package being
out of sync in the package repository when the images were built. This
will be fixed tomorrow when I'll built another set of images.

The images can be found in [1]. Please test!

Thanks,
Adrian

> [1] https://cdimage.debian.org/cdimage/ports/snapshots/2025-03-31/

